# JavaScript Code Cleanup Standards

Standards for writing clean, maintainable JavaScript code.

<rule>
name: javascript_code_cleanup
description: Guidelines for writing clean JavaScript code following best practices

filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.js$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?s).*function.*|.*const.*|.*let.*|.*var.*"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When writing JavaScript code:

      1. Function Guidelines:
         - Start with a verb (e.g., get, set, create, update)
         - Use camelCase
         - Keep functions short (<20 instructions)
         - Add JSDoc comments for all functions
         - Use early returns to avoid nesting
         - Use arrow functions for simple operations (<3 lines)
         ```javascript
         // Bad
         function getData() {
           if (condition) {
             if (otherCondition) {
               return data;
             }
           }
         }

         // Good
         function getData() {
           if (!condition) return null;
           if (!otherCondition) return null;
           return data;
         }
         ```

      2. Naming Conventions:
         - PascalCase for classes
         - camelCase for variables/functions
         - Use complete words (except standard abbr.)
         - Boolean variables start with is/has/can
         - Event handlers start with handle
         ```javascript
         // Bad
         let usr = {};
         function procData() {}
         
         // Good
         let user = {};
         function processData() {}
         ```

      3. State Management:
         - Group related state in objects
         - Use const by default
         - Minimize global state
         ```javascript
         // Bad
         let container = null;
         let model = null;
         
         // Good
         const appState = {
           container: null,
           model: null
         };
         ```

      4. Error Handling:
         - Use descriptive error messages
         - Add validation at function start
         - Use early returns for validation
         ```javascript
         // Bad
         if (!model) throw new Error("Invalid");
         
         // Good
         if (!model) {
           throw new Error("Model must be initialized before operation");
         }
         ```

examples:
  - input: |
      function getData(id) {
        if (id) {
          if (cache[id]) {
            return cache[id];
          }
        }
        return null;
      }

    output: |
      /**
       * Retrieves data for the given ID from cache
       * @param {string} id The ID to look up
       * @returns {Object|null} The cached data or null if not found
       */
      function getData(id) {
        if (!id) return null;
        return cache[id] || null;
      }

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
  tags:
    - javascript
    - cleanup
    - best-practices
</rule>